<title>USA: Barnes &amp; Noble Inc holiday sales rise.</title>
<headline>Barnes &amp; Noble Inc holiday sales rise.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Percent change</p>
<p>		    1996	 1995	     Total     Same-Store</p>
<p>Nine weeks	$654.0     $564.5	 +16	 +8.8</p>
<p>Year-to-date    $2,261     $1,859	 +22	 +7.1</p>
<p>NOTE: Figures in millions except percentage.</p>
<p>    Period is   nine weeks ended	   Jan 4.</p>
<p>Figures are for total revenues, except same-store figures, which are for the company's superstores and include store relocations.</p>
<p>Superstore same-store sales excluding store relocations rose 5.6 pct in nine-week period and rose 5.1 pct year-to-date.</p>
<p>Mall stores comparable-store sales fell 3.8 pct for nine-week period and fell 7.7 pct year-to-date.</p>
</text>
